  "notes": "USAGE:\n{投|な}げつける implies forceful, often aggressive throwing directed at a specific target. It is stronger than simply ⟦{投|な}げる→投げる：01135_nageru⟧ (to throw). Figuratively, it is used with words, insults, or accusations.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nIchidan (ru-verb). Transitive. The target is marked with ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧, and the thrown object with ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{石|いし}→石：02177_ishi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{投|な}げつける (to throw a stone at)\n- ⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{投|な}げつける (to hurl words at)\n- ⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{投|な}げつける (to fling one's anger at)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{投|な}げる→投げる：01135_nageru⟧: to throw (neutral, general)\n- ⟦ぶつける→ぶつける：02413_butsukeru⟧: to hit, to throw against (focus on impact)",
